 "method": "Sentinel-2 L2A surface reflectance (ESA Copernicus, via Element 84 Earth Search on AWS; Collection-1 reprocessing, original L2A archive where Collection 1 has no scenes), 10 m. Box: 6 x 6 km centred on the Garuda Palace (OpenStreetMap position). Per period: up to 8 of the least cloudy days; pixels kept only where the Sen2Cor scene classification (SCL) says vegetation, bare/built or water; per-pixel median NDVI over the clear observations. Vegetated = NDVI > 0.6, bare or built = NDVI < 0.3. cleared_since_baseline_ha = pixels vegetated in the baseline (Jan - 25 Aug 2019, before the 26 Aug 2019 announcement) and bare/built in that period. CAVEATS: much of the zone was an industrial eucalyptus/acacia plantation (not natural forest) before 2019, so 'vegetation' includes plantation trees and some clearing comes from plantation harvest cycles, not only construction. Sen2Cor sometimes calls bright new roofs and concrete 'cloud', which removes them from a day (the median uses the other days). Ground in between NDVI 0.3 and 0.6 (grass, young regrowth, landscaped lawns) counts as neither."
}